{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The guard sorts a new slice of pointers and doesn’t mutate the cached graph. Its path selection, base revision, and error handling match the previous code. The probe cache also leaves execution cleanup unchanged: dispatch still calls the real group verifier.\n\nThe spec accepts up to one minute of stale capability reporting if `/proc` access changes. The reported speedup rests on two alternating runs with competing machine load, so I treat its size as approximate. I’m using sealed test results because this sandbox cannot build or write test fixtures."}}
